---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../site.js';
---
<Legal title="Privacy Policy" description="Draft privacy policy for YuktiOps: what we collect, why, and how long we keep it.">
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>YuktiOps ("we") provides server and website monitoring. [Legal entity name, registered address and country to be added.] Contact: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account data:</strong> your name, email address and a hashed password, your organization name, and the teammates you invite.</li>
    <li><strong>Monitoring data:</strong> server statistics sent by the agent (see <a href="/security">what the agent collects</a>), the results of website and API checks, and alert history.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP addresses and basic logs for security and abuse prevention.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment data:</strong> when billing is enabled, payments are handled by Razorpay or Stripe. We do not store card numbers.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <p>To run the service, send alerts, keep it secure, support you and, where required, meet legal and tax duties. We do not sell your data.</p>
  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Monitoring data is kept for the history length of your plan (7 days to 1 year) and then deleted. Account data is kept while your account is open. [Retention after deletion to be confirmed.]</p>
  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>Service providers that help us run YuktiOps (hosting, email delivery, payments, and the messaging services you choose for alerts such as Telegram or Slack). [List of providers and their locations to be completed.]</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask to see, correct, export or delete your data. Write to us at the address above. [Applicable laws, such as India's DPDP Act and GDPR, to be addressed by counsel.]</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy we will update this page and, for important changes, email you.</p>
</Legal>
